SUMMARY:[Hike - Difficult] Seaton Trail & 3rd Concession
DESCRIPTION:GTA Hiking & Stuff\nValley Farm Dog Park @ Seaton Trail & 3rd 
 Concession -\n**\\*\\*\\* This is a difficult trail \\*\\*\\***\n\nPlease 
 read carefully to maximize the enjoyment of everyone who attends:\n\nThere
  are multiple trails located here\, some are relatively easy\, others are 
 more difficult. I will be leading you over the more challenging sections a
 nd at a fast pace. We wont be running\, but moving along quickly. Don't wo
 rry\, we will be stopping to rest at the peaks as well as some of the more
  scenic areas.\n\nThis area contains a number of rather steep hills which 
 tend to be rocky and wet. Flip side\, this trail also offers gorgeous view
 s both from the peaks\, as well as down along the water.\n\nWe will hike a
 t a medium pace (4 - 5 km/h) for the 10 or so kms.\n\nIt's not a hike for 
 beginners due to the steep rocky hills and faster pace. For the same reaso
 n no dogs or children.\n\nBring 1L of water and good hiking shoes or boots
 .\n\nParking Address:\nValley Farm Rd. & 3rd Concession · Pickering\, ON\
 n\nNOTE: Due to construction you can’t take Brock to 3rd concession\, yo
 u MUST take valley farm road which you can reach from Brock via Dellbrook 
 Ave\, or alternatively via Kingston or Finch Ave.\n\nThere are signs warni
 ng of construction\, the trail and parking are open so just follow the con
 struction signs. At the end of valley farm turn LEFT - The parking lot is 
 not far and on your left.\n\n***Hike starts at 9:30-am SHARP.***\n\nDetail
 s from the last time I did this hike:\n\nDistance : 8.87 km\nMoving Time :
  1:57:53\nElapsed Time : 2:33:38\nPace : 13:17 /km\n\n**LEGAL DISCLAIMER A
 ND LIABILITY INFORMATION:**\nBy RSVP'ing and paying the event fee (if appl
 icable)\, you are confirming that you have read\, understand and accept th
 e following:\n\n1. GTA Hiking Meetup is a private group. Attending events 
 is voluntary by you as a member. Participation in any activity with us is 
 at your own risk.\n2. By joining this event as a member you agree to indem
 nify and hold harmless its organizers\, co-organizers\, assistant organize
 rs\, event hosts\, and other members from all claims or liability of every
  type (including court costs and legal fees) for injury or death to any pe
 rson or for damage to property\, loss of personal property or any other wr
 ongful act arising out of or relating to your participation as a member. T
 his agreement applies to you and to other persons (as your guests) who may
  accompany you in these endeavours.\n3. You also agree to hold the organiz
 ers as well as other group members harmless. By participating voluntarily 
 in the group\, you expressly waive any and all such claims against each an
 d every other member in the group\, including without limitation any and a
 ll claims against the group organizer\, co-organizers\, assistant organize
 rs\, and event hosts.\n\n**TICK WARNING**\nTicks are small bugs that can a
 ttach to skin and sometimes spread illnesses like Lyme disease. Learn more
  at:\n[https://www.canada.ca/en/public-health/services/diseases/lyme-disea
 se/prevention-lyme-disease.html](https://www.canada.ca/en/public-health/se
 rvices/diseases/lyme-disease/prevention-lyme-disease.html)
