SUMMARY:Seaton Trail - After Work Hike\, Intermediate
DESCRIPTION:GTA Hiking & Stuff\nAfter work hikes are a series of cardio hi
 kes to get us in shape for the summer season. This will be a faster hike\,
  so please know your limits as breaks will be minimal.\n\nWe will hike nor
 th for an hour at a moderate pace with the goal of making it to the Whitev
 ale parking lot before turning back. The hike will cover aprox. 9 km in 2 
 hrs or less. We should be done before nightfall\, but a flashlight may be 
 a good idea.\n\nThe trail weaves through the forest and along a creek. The
 re will be twists and turns and ups and downs\, but nothing serious.\n\n**
 Note**\n• Arrive on time! Don't let the group wait for you.\n• Know yo
 ur limits! Hike within it!\n• Dress for the conditions.\n• Free Parkin
 g\n• No Dogs\n• The hike will be canceled if the weather doesn't coope
 rate.\n\n***Hike leaves promptly at 6:07 PM***\n\nHope to see you there!\n
 \n**LEGAL DISCLAIMER AND LIABILITY INFORMATION:**\n\nBy RSVP'ing and payin
 g the event fee (if applicable)\, you are confirming that you have read\, 
 understand and accept the following:\n\n1. GTA Hiking Meetup is a private 
 group. Attending events is voluntary by you as a member. Participation in 
 any activity with us is at your own risk.\n2. By joining this event as a m
 ember you agree to indemnify and hold harmless its organizers\, co-organiz
 ers\, assistant organizers\, event hosts\, and other members from all clai
 ms or liability of every type (including court costs and legal fees) for i
 njury or death to any person or for damage to property\, loss of personal 
 property or any other wrongful act arising out of or relating to your part
 icipation as a member. This agreement applies to you and to other persons 
 (as your guests) who may accompany you in these endeavors.\n3. You also ag
 ree to hold the organizers as well as other group members harmless. By par
 ticipating voluntarily in the group\, you expressly waive any and all such
  claims against each and every other member in the group\, including witho
 ut limitation any and all claims against the group organizer\, co-organize
 rs\, assistant organizers\, and event hosts.
